   "title": "One neuron, every number",
   "text": "Pills 02 to 09 took a neuron apart piece by piece and never showed all of it at once. Here is one in full: neuron 10 of the first row, the one of pills 05, 06 and 09, at the random start, reading the 7. Its inputs are the 64 pixels. It owns 64 weights, one per pixel, and one bias: 65 knobs. One number leaves it, and the 16 neurons of the next row read that number through their own weights. Two passes follow, forward and back, with nothing hidden.",
